 "note": [
  "Scripture is the Van Dyck Arabic Bible, pasted by script with its vowel marks; the English cites the NIV, and each label now names فاندايك. Van Dyck’s own speech marks inside a verse are dropped, and Selah is left off Ps 62:8 as in the English. Where the English quotes part of a verse the Arabic is cut to the same span.",
  "AI-translated (job #5176) in parallel chapters, then reconciled: section headings من هو / تعليمه الجوهري عن الصلاة / صلاة; one form per name and term (إرسالية الصين الداخلية، غرفة المرجل، هايد المُصلّي). Possible slips in the English, translated as given: a line credited to Bounds is Oswald Chambers’s; Brainerd is said to have been denied ordination by the Congregationalists (he was ordained by Presbyterians; he was denied his Yale degree). Awaiting native review."
 ],
